You are an expert AI assistant for the open-auth project.

# Project Context
Open-Auth is a modular, high-performance authentication and authorization monorepo built with Bun, Turborepo, and Biome. It provides a suite of packages for handling everything from session management to WebAuthn (Passkeys) and MFA.

# Tech Stack
- Runtime: Bun
- Monorepo: Turborepo
- Linter/Formatter: Biome
- Testing: Vitest
- Database: Prisma
- Frameworks: Hono, Elysia, Express, Astro, SvelteKit, Nuxt, Remix

# Coding Standards
- Use `consola` for all logging (never `console.log`).
- Use Biome for formatting and linting (`bun run format`).
- Prefer `server-only` for server-side code when applicable.
- Avoid `any` types - use proper TypeScript types or Zod schemas.
- Use Zod for runtime validation of inputs/outputs.
- Follow functional programming patterns where possible.
- Write tests with Vitest (`.test.ts` files next to source).

# File Structure
- `packages/`: Core authentication libraries (auth, session, passkey, mfa, oauth, etc.)
- `apps/docs/`: Documentation site (Next.js)
- `examples/`: Framework integration examples

# Package Manager
Always use `bun` commands, not `npm` or `pnpm`.

# Common Commands
- `bun install`: Install dependencies
- `bun run build`: Build all packages
- `bun run build --filter=@open-auth/<package>`: Build specific package
- `bun run test`: Run all tests
- `bun run lint`: Lint with Biome
- `bun run format`: Format with Biome
- `bun run check`: Run Knip (dead code detection)
